{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Why\n\nDebugging-orchestration sessions periodically sweep for AWS + GitHub Actions errors\n\"since the last sweep.\" Passing the last-sweep timeline across sessions needs a durable,\nzero-noise carrier. We already use a dedicated long-lived `session_log` ticket\n(`tomophobic-stilllife-mayfly` / `b2dc-b1ab-0bd9-47f6`, tagged `ops-sweep`) as an\nappend-only ledger, but the convention is undocumented, so future sessions cannot\nreliably discover or extend it. `session_log` is the right carrier precisely because it\nis excluded from default `list`, `ready`/`next-batch`, and graph-health, and never syncs\nto Jira — an always-open ledger creates zero work-queue noise.\n\n## What\n\nDocument the \"ops error-sweep ledger\" convention in the docs and add a one-line pointer\nin AGENTS.md so debug sessions discover it. This is a DOCS-ONLY change — no source or\ntest code is touched.\n\n- `docs/user-guide.md`: add a new subsection (e.g. \"### Ops error-sweep ledger\") in/after\n  the existing \"## Session logs\" section, matching that section's concise, example-driven\n  style. Cover: the ledger is a `session_log` ticket (and why — queue/graph/Jira\n  exclusion); the current ledger id/alias + `ops-sweep` tag; discovery via\n  `rebar search \"ops-sweep\"`; the newest comment / `SWEEP <ISO-8601> | window <start>..<end>`\n  header convention and next-window rule; appending with `rebar comment <ledger-id>` (NOT\n  `session-log append`, which is session-keyed and auto-rotates); linking filed tickets\n  with `rebar link <filed> <ledger-id> relates_to` (non-blocking relations only); and how\n  to recreate the ledger (`session-log start` + `tag ... ops-sweep`), with the tag+search\n  as the durable anchor.\n- `AGENTS.md`: extend ONLY the existing one-line \"Session logs\" pointer bullet under\n  \"Where to read\" to mention the ops error-sweep ledger convention. Keep it a pointer, not\n  restated content (AGENTS.md policy: already-documented topics are one-line pointers into\n  docs/).\n\n## Scope\n\n- Files: `docs/user-guide.md` (new subsection), `AGENTS.md` (one-line pointer extension).\n- Out of scope: any code/test change; restating the full convention in AGENTS.md.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [x] `docs/user-guide.md` has a new subsection under \"## Session logs\" documenting the\n      ops error-sweep ledger convention accurately: session_log rationale, ledger id/alias\n      + `ops-sweep` tag, discovery via search, the `SWEEP ... | window ...` header +\n      next-window rule, append via `rebar comment` (not `session-log append`), link via\n      `relates_to`, and recreation via `session-log start` + tag.\n- [x] `AGENTS.md`'s existing \"Session logs\" pointer bullet is extended by one line/clause\n      to mention the ops error-sweep ledger convention — a pointer only, no restated body.\n- [x] The convention text matches the mechanics in docs/event-schema.md (\"The session_log\n      ticket type\") and docs/user-guide.md (\"Session logs\") — no contradictions.\n- [x] `make lint` passes; no new tooling added; no source/test files changed."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1788287445100857001,"uuid":"0f412f6d-efcc-458e-9462-05949179e3c0"}